{"post_stream": {"posts": [{"id": 230931, "name": "Anatoli Babenia", "username": "abitrolly", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/abitrolly/{size}/964_2.png", "created_at": "2023-07-12T06:15:48.807Z", "cooked": "<p>I’ve run out of space on <code>/</code> and discovered that Flatpak is a space hog.</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/fedoraproject/original/3X/c/7/c7c85ce1fd80af2dd4cf055a4cecf62fd79abf17.png\" alt=\"image\" data-base62-sha1=\"svmi6p39faa32pDob8PV7MZIPj1\" width=\"690\" height=\"105\"></p>\n<p>I don’t have really much things installed. Most of them are some dependencies, among which is 2.7Gb of Fedora. Why? Why promote such inefficient distribution method that can not even take advantage of the already installed binary blobs?</p>\n<pre><code class=\"lang-auto\">s flatpak list --columns name,size\nName                                               Installed size\nShortwave                                            8,2 MB\nKooha                                                4,9 MB\nAudacity                                            58,0 MB\nFedora Platform                                      2,7 GB\nMesa                                               424,2 MB\nMesa (Extra)                                       424,2 MB\nIntel                                               46,5 MB\nopenh264                                           790,0 kB\nGNU Image Manipulation Program                     252,8 MB\nGNOME Application Platform version 43              864,0 MB\nGNOME Application Platform version 44              860,6 MB\n</code></pre>", "post_number": 1, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 5, "updated_at": "2023-07-12T06:15:48.807Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 1399, "reads": 56, "readers_count": 55, "score": 7001.2, "yours": false, "topic_id": 85652, "topic_slug": "flatpak-is-eating-too-much-space-and-duplicates-fedora-files", "display_username": "Anatoli Babenia", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": null, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 958, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 1, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/flatpak-is-eating-too-much-space-and-duplicates-fedora-files/85652/1", "event": null, "calendar_details": [], "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 230935, "name": "Sakiko Togawa", "username": "yuntaz", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/yuntaz/{size}/44300_2.png", "created_at": "2023-07-12T06:48:50.419Z", "cooked": "<p>Would you be able to determine the runtime being utilized by executing the following command in a shell environment?</p>\n<pre><code class=\"lang-sh\">flatpak list --columns=name,runtime,size\n</code></pre>\n<p>This command will display a list of installed Flatpak applications along with their respective runtime and size. In some cases, you can remove Fedora Platform because it is pinned but not used by any apps.</p>", "post_number": 2, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 5, "updated_at": "2023-07-12T06:48:50.419Z", "reply_count": 1, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 16, "reads": 55, "readers_count": 54, "score": 96.0, "yours": false, "topic_id": 85652, "topic_slug": "flatpak-is-eating-too-much-space-and-duplicates-fedora-files", "display_username": "Sakiko Togawa", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": "Curious Penguin (Ask Fedora IV)", "title_is_group": false, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 12407, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 2, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/flatpak-is-eating-too-much-space-and-duplicates-fedora-files/85652/2", "event": null, "reactions": [{"id": "bluethumb", "type": "emoji", "count": 1}], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 1, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 230953, "name": "Anatoli Babenia", "username": "abitrolly", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/abitrolly/{size}/964_2.png", "created_at": "2023-07-12T08:42:21.242Z", "cooked": "<p>Fedora was used by Audacity, so I removed it. The rest of the list.</p>\n<pre><code class=\"lang-auto\">$ flatpak list --columns=name,runtime,size \nName                                                Runtime                                   Installed size\nShortwave                                           org.gnome.Platform/x86_64/44                8,2 MB\nKooha                                               org.gnome.Platform/x86_64/43                4,9 MB\nMesa                                                                                          424,2 MB\nMesa (Extra)                                                                                  424,2 MB\nIntel                                                                                          46,5 MB\nopenh264                                                                                      790,0 kB\nGNU Image Manipulation Program                      org.gnome.Platform/x86_64/44              254,4 MB\nGNOME Application Platform version 43                                                         864,0 MB\nGNOME Application Platform version 44                                                         860,6 MB\n</code></pre>\n<p>It looks like Mesa is removable, but it is not.</p>\n<pre><code class=\"lang-auto\">Info: applications using the extension org.freedesktop.Platform.GL.default branch 22.08:\n   io.github.seadve.Kooha, de.haeckerfelix.Shortwave, org.gimp.GIMP\n</code></pre>", "post_number": 3, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 5, "updated_at": "2023-07-12T08:42:21.242Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": 2, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 11, "reads": 50, "readers_count": 49, "score": 65.0, "yours": false, "topic_id": 85652, "topic_slug": "flatpak-is-eating-too-much-space-and-duplicates-fedora-files", "display_username": "Anatoli Babenia", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": null, "reply_to_user": {"id": 12407, "username": "yuntaz", "name": "Sakiko Togawa", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/yuntaz/{size}/44300_2.png"}, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 958, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 1, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/flatpak-is-eating-too-much-space-and-duplicates-fedora-files/85652/3", "event": null, "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 230965, "name": "Sakiko Togawa", "username": "yuntaz", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/yuntaz/{size}/44300_2.png", "created_at": "2023-07-12T09:29:40.082Z", "cooked": "<p>Mesa is not removable. If you want to free up space, try removing other unused packages with the following command:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"lang-sh\">flatpak remove --unused\n</code></pre>\n<p>Moreover, if you still wish to use Audacity, you can reinstall it without the Fedora platform. This can be done using the command below, which explicitly tells Flatpak to acquire Audacity from the <code>flathub</code> repository:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"lang-sh\">flatpak install flathub org.audacityteam.Audacity\n</code></pre>\n<p>When installing a Flatpak app, you’re sometimes asked if you want to install it from the <code>fedora</code> repository or the <code>flathub</code> repository. If you choose <code>fedora</code>, Flatpak will install the Fedora platform runtime, which can consume more space than desired. This is why you might prefer installing from <code>flathub</code> instead.</p>\n<pre><code class=\"lang-auto\">flatpak install org.audacityteam.Audacity\nLooking for matches…\nRemotes found with refs similar to ‘org.audacityteam.Audacity’:\n\n   1) ‘fedora’ (system)\n   2) ‘flathub’ (system)\n\nWhich do you want to use (0 to abort)? [0-2]:\n</code></pre>\n<p>If you want to avoid this issue in the future, consider disabling the Fedora repository permanently. You can do this in Gnome Software by navigating to Software Repositories. KDE Discover should have a similar setting.</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/fedoraproject/original/3X/e/1/e13df2cac90936e6473e8e1394cb97523f3bb05f.png\" alt=\"Screenshot from 2023-07-12 02-16-34\" data-base62-sha1=\"w8A9AFr5McBVEmd9K1HKmR94oYD\" width=\"626\" height=\"392\"></p>", "post_number": 4, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 5, "updated_at": "2023-07-12T09:30:57.435Z", "reply_count": 1, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 42, "reads": 44, "readers_count": 43, "score": 223.8, "yours": false, "topic_id": 85652, "topic_slug": "flatpak-is-eating-too-much-space-and-duplicates-fedora-files", "display_username": "Sakiko Togawa", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": "Curious Penguin (Ask Fedora IV)", "title_is_group": false, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 12407, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 2, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/flatpak-is-eating-too-much-space-and-duplicates-fedora-files/85652/4", "event": null, "reactions": [{"id": "bluethumb", "type": "emoji", "count": 1}], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 1, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 230980, "name": "Anatoli Babenia", "username": "abitrolly", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/abitrolly/{size}/964_2.png", "created_at": "2023-07-12T12:52:34.741Z", "cooked": "<p>Disabled these repos permanently. Overall I don’t think Flatpaks is a good packaging solution. Better leverage <a href=\"https://github.com/whalebrew/whalebrew\" class=\"inline-onebox\">GitHub - whalebrew/whalebrew: Homebrew, but with Docker images</a> with <code>podman</code> and convert those Flatpak definitions into more secure and less space hungry containers.</p>", "post_number": 5, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 5, "updated_at": "2023-07-12T12:52:34.741Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": 4, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 18, "reads": 40, "readers_count": 39, "score": 98.0, "yours": false, "topic_id": 85652, "topic_slug": "flatpak-is-eating-too-much-space-and-duplicates-fedora-files", "display_username": "Anatoli Babenia", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "link_counts": [{"url": "https://github.com/whalebrew/whalebrew", "internal": false, "reflection": false, "title": "GitHub - whalebrew/whalebrew: Homebrew, but with Docker images", "clicks": 55}], "read": true, "user_title": null, "reply_to_user": {"id": 12407, "username": "yuntaz", "name": "Sakiko Togawa", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/yuntaz/{size}/44300_2.png"}, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 958, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 1, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/flatpak-is-eating-too-much-space-and-duplicates-fedora-files/85652/5", "event": null, "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}], "stream": [230931, 230935, 230953, 230965, 230980]}, "timeline_lookup": [[1, 1211]], "suggested_topics": [], "tags": [{"id": 297, "name": "engineering", "slug": "engineering"}], "tags_descriptions": {"engineering": "General topics relating to Fedora Project eng